#:layer #!pragmatics

@plan: ~"./PLAN.md"
@index: ~"./index.spw"
@wip_notebook: ~"../../../.spw/conventions/wip-notebook.spw"
@model: ~"./blog-blob-spw.spw"
@blog_index: ~"../../../blog/index.html"
@ways_cache: ~"../../../.spw/caches/ways-2026-10.spw"

operation = "cache"
fixity = "tending"

^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-12 10:59] verify — the Status holds. blog/ still has only index.html: no post folder and no starter.spw, and scripts/blog-weave.mjs and a blog:weave script do not exist, as planned. The first post waits on its subject, which is the creator's to name and write.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:58] verify — blog/ still holds only index.html; since 10-10 it changed in 3a009a35 (the workbench's operator names on its cards) and b5171318 (its Spw blocks highlighted). No starter.spw, no scripts/blog-weave.mjs, no blog:weave script. The ways cache's practices line says November writing feeds starters, and edf0344a puts November's book for lore.land on Home and /now/, chapters on Sundays, outlines held.
 >>[2026-11-06 13:00] plan — the first-post wonder gains a hypothesis, an expect and an answer set (post.november_book, post.a_season_expression, post.creators_other_subject); the subject stays the creator's. PLAN.md's Files list drops the two [NEW] lines that landed and keeps only the files a real starter would touch.
}

^"open"{
 first_post = ~"./index.spw#wonder_blog_blob_spw_first_post"
}

^"cache"{
 ~#status: "waiting"
 ~#next_commit: "+[blog] Publish the first post, readable with scripts off, with its starter beside it and one dated feeding"
 ~#files_hot: "blog/index.html, .agents/plans/blog-blob-spw/blog-blob-spw.spw, .spw/caches/ways-2026-10.spw"
 ~#gate: "the creator's first post: its subject and its words"
 ~#last_stream: "2026-11-06"
}
